  "precedence": "The focused owner-confirmed Food overlay supersedes incompatible Food proposals and adds the Food step, Task, meals and hunger. The 13 November Hold, 50/200/150 ms timing, single kill-and-deliver path, hunger order and remaining timing approvals supersede earlier Food drafts. All unsuperseded parent rules and original source pins remain inherited. The later 13 November owner adoption closes the four Hold continuation proposals. Prototype wire semantics remain design evidence, not executable authority. Later 13 November owner decision: a Captain killed after leaving Command returns at the unchanged common boundary under inherited Captain-loss A/B fallback, rather than occupying C1 as a body.",
